("api/add-tree-root" :names ("add-tree-root") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Require empty tree; create/select root silently under native event blockers and publish checked token/view. Empty text valid. Failed Lisp view publication deletes new native item." :position 15026)
("api/allow-next-key-event" :names ("allow-next-key-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Calls DoAllowNextEvent on current CHAR_HOOK context; keeps hook consumption independent from normal key generation." :position 16228)
("api/append-item" :names ("append-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Append native text silently, preserving selected index/NIL. Empty strings/duplicates allowed. Native failure signals; no transactional rollback claim." :position 17500)
("api/append-tree-item" :names ("append-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Append in native order, preserving selection silently. Native parent owner is inferred and checked; empty/duplicate text valid." :position 18514)
("api/application-handler" :names ("application-handler") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Borrowed native identity with inherited binding, dispatch, liveness and enabled state. Direct construction and subclass construction are rejected; explicit destruction signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup owns the native wxApp." :position 19640)
("api/aui-notebook" :names ("aui-notebook") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed dynamic panel-page container, native programmatic tab splitting and fixed top/close styles, with at most256 pages. Mouse reordering is available while one group exists; split books use checked programmatic movement. Direct subclasses/default initargs/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback." :position 21165)
("api/begin-stc-undo-action" :names ("begin-stc-undo-action") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native BeginUndoAction. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 23772)
("api/bind-event" :names ("bind-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Register an observer without replacing any existing generic or control-specific registration. Signed 32-bit IDs are supported except -1 (reserved as native wxID_ANY; use NIL). LAST-ID requires ID and an ordered inclusive range. Observer bindings automatically Skip; contextual bindings start unskipped and control native Skip explicitly; relative callback order follows wxWidgets and is not a Lisp API guarantee. Failed registration releases temporary roots. Contextual access is limited to the innermost callback and expires at return, including on errors. A native entry-owned wxObject token adapter represents non-NIL user data without a Lisp/native pointer. EVENT-USER-DATA reads the per-binding value in snapshots/current contexts; there is no public mutation API for an existing association. ABI37 adds :NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGING/:NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGED notify-family observers/contexts. Only CHANGING veto affects navigation. Native page callbacks protect the originating book/ancestors and reject same-book recursive selection, modal and clipboard entry. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits. ABI39 tree selection changing/changed are native-only wxTreeEvent notify types. EVENT-TREE-ITEM captures canonical view identity, not frozen text/validity; same-tree writes and nested native loops defer until callback return." :position 24822)
("api/binding-active-p" :names ("binding-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session registration and reap stale generic callback roots. Root pruning also runs at returned RUN/pump/notifying-setter boundaries and after explicit destruction. During a blocking RUN, native window closure may retain roots until a Lisp boundary or explicit unbinding. This does not change the control-specific callback-root contract." :position 32317)
("api/button" :names ("button") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxButton with click handler support." :position 34085)
("api/calendar-date" :names ("calendar-date" "(setf calendar-date)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Local civil date without exposed time-of-day/timezone/Unix/universal-time. Gregorian leap/day/range validation; native construction/readback must preserve requested date. Native getter with no supported committed date signals NATIVE-ERROR." :position 35218)
("api/call-with-application" :names ("call-with-application") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Initialize a main-thread GUI session, call FUNCTION, and clean up on normal return or unwinding. RUN is explicit." :position 37174)
("api/cancel-stc-autocomplete" :names ("cancel-stc-autocomplete") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native AutoCompCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 38012)
("api/cancel-stc-call-tip" :names ("cancel-stc-call-tip") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native CallTipCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 39066)
("api/cancel-ui-action" :names ("cancel-ui-action") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove queued work and release its Lisp closure root. Cannot interrupt active work; owner expiry may already have pruned it." :position 40106)
("api/cancel-ui-timer" :names ("cancel-ui-timer") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Stop native notifications, remove coalesced due work and release its root. Current periodic function can cancel itself; cannot interrupt an executing function." :position 41259)
("api/canvas-client-size" :names ("canvas-client-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Get native client size through ToDIP. Integer scaling may round by a pixel. Resize repaints retained data but does not rewrite the model; applications can rebuild geometry from this value. Reports retained native paint failure before returning." :position 42412)
("api/canvas-content" :names ("canvas-content" "(setf canvas-content)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Items are (:rect x y width height rgb), (:ellipse x y width height rgb), (:line x1 y1 x2 y2 rgb stroke-width), (:text x y string point-size rgb), or (:bitmap x y width height pixels). RGB bytes0..255, coordinates/endpoints ±10000, non-bitmap extents1..10000, line widths1..32, text6..72 points in native Swiss/sans family. Text is NUL/CR/LF-free, total65536 UTF-8 bytes; bitmaps1..256 per axis use exact simple RGB byte vectors, total2MiB. On-screen geometry uses DIP; no alpha/native resource handles." :position 43687)
("api/checkbox" :names ("checkbox") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a two-state wxCheckBox." :position 46368)
