("api/pending-events-p" :names ("pending-events-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks." :position 388858)
("api/pop-event-handler" :names ("pop-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions." :position 389966)
("api/post-event" :names ("post-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session." :position 391929)
("api/previous-handler" :names ("previous-handler" "(setf previous-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent." :position 393547)
("api/process-event" :names ("process-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 395692)
("api/process-event-locally" :names ("process-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode." :position 400125)
("api/process-events" :names ("process-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling." :position 402323)
("api/process-pending-events" :names ("process-pending-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards." :position 403329)
("api/process-window-event" :names ("process-window-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary." :position 404964)
("api/process-window-event-locally" :names ("process-window-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only." :position 406915)
("api/pulse-gauge" :names ("pulse-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode." :position 409082)
("api/push-event-handler" :names ("push-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation." :position 410369)
("api/queue-click" :names ("queue-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement." :position 412238)
("api/queue-event" :names ("queue-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 413213)
("api/radio-box" :names ("radio-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods." :position 418203)
("api/realize-toolbar" :names ("realize-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator." :position 419447)
("api/register-event-type" :names ("register-event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes." :position 420374)
("api/remove-event-handler" :names ("remove-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion." :position 422116)
