("api/return-to-application-repl" :names ("return-to-application-repl") :kind :restart :kind-name "Restart" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart." :position 433342)
("api/run" :names ("run") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code." :position 434153)
("api/run-web-script" :names ("run-web-script") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Asynchronously evaluates JavaScript. JSON-fragment success (undefined maps to null), native error or non-serializable result failure arrives through :web-script-result. Results over1MiB become an error. Ticket retires before event callbacks. Messages posted to window.webkit.messageHandlers.wxlambda.postMessage(value) arrive as JSON via :web-message; at most256 queued messages, each up to1MiB, excess dropped. Owner teardown drops late completions. Queued immutable command snapshots: :web-message text is JSON (including quoted strings); :web-script-result text is JSON on success or an error description on failure, EVENT-INTEGER is1/0 and EVENT-EXTRA-LONG is the request ticket; :web-loaded text is native URL and :web-error text is native error description. BIND-EVENT supports scoped contexts/Skip/propagation but payload SETF rejects. Async delivery occurs through normal GUI polling/RUN, never directly from an Objective-C completion. Native loaded/error events can reflect prior/subframe navigation; no exact per-navigation correlation or veto API." :position 435064)
("api/save-canvas-image" :names ("save-canvas-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Render same retained scene into private RGB24 bitmap and PNG. Export coordinates are pixels, one scene unit per pixel with clipping, not model scaling; fonts keep native point-size metrics. Internal PNG handler does not alter global registry. Existing target is overwritten; encoding is staged before open, but write/flush/close failure can leave partial output and is not atomic replacement." :position 438707)
